# RETIRED: the scene this restores cannot play. The director has receivers [87] but nothing in the game
# carries 87 at it; it has no slot 1, so TriggerLinkedObjects cannot reach it (that command is
# ExecuteEvent with index 1, and an event index is a script slot); and its slot-0 DEFAULT script goes
# nowhere. Independently, arrival_test reports NOT TRIGGERED for labint and neither of that level's two
# triggers targets the director. See tools/scene_survey.py, which checks all three routes.
#
# NOT VERIFIED: the scene this restores has never been observed playing, and the run that appeared to verify it
# was measuring the Iceberg Lab *movie* instead. labint has two triggers - an FMV player and a door - and neither
# targets the director (instance 1), so a plain warp cannot start it: arrival_test says NOT TRIGGERED, and the
# FMV trigger at (-14.34, -2.85, -10.33) gives 55.7s -> 4.0s with this recipe built in and 55.7s -> 4.0s without
# it, because what hold-Triangle is skipping there is the movie, which the executable patch already skips.
# cutscene_test now labels a run 'movie' or 'scene' so that cannot be misread again. Ship this only once the
# in-engine scene has been seen playing.
#
# Iceberg Lab interior (H02B); skip runs COM_ICELABINT_CUTSCENE_SKIP
file Levels\Ice\Hub\labint.rm2
copybody 6237 1 5 0 3 572 1 0   # COM_ICELABINT_CUTSCENE_DIRECTOR_ACTIVATED: state 1 plays the cutscene; add the developers' Triangle rule (cond 572, player 1) -> state 3
clearbodies 6237 5                  # drop the unreachable original in state 5
